<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.11.5: Graphs of Quadratic Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01933</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.11.5: Graphs of Quadratic Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3034a28b-b25a-417f-9fcb-f6492af1bf6f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>The function \(f\) is given by \(f(x)=(x-2)(x+4)\). </para>
<para>Without using graphing technology, answer questions 1 – 4.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph representing \(f\)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x\)-intercepts for function \(f\): \((2,0)\) and \((-4,0)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="3ef6b782-dbe3-4cae-a77c-9770e9a31299"><problem><para>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:<emphasis/></para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>-1</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is -1.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-8)\), because \((0-2)(0+4)=(-2)(4)=-8\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Sketch a graph that represents \(f\).</para>
    <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>The graph opens upward with vertex at \((-1,-9)\) and \(x\)-intercepts at \((2,0)\) and \((-4, 0)\).</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/881615b7474f3ba14c771ce12346fe82e703bc6d"/></media></figure></para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
